[agent] ## Summary
[agent] I produced the training dataset `churntrainingb2a26a`, version 1 on the platform, but it **cannot meet the "exactly these columns" requirement** due to a missing capability in the CLI. Here's the full picture.
[agent] ### What I did (all on-platform via `hops`)
[agent] 1. **Audited the pre-existing feature groups.** Five FGs already existed (`transactions`, `profiles`, `activity`, `account_health`, `labels`), each with the right schema and event-time column. Via `fg stats`/`preview` I found `profiles` (165), `activity` (1300), `account_health` (200), and `labels` (100) were complete, but **`transactions` held only 65 rows — exactly `transactions_late.csv`, with the initial `transactions.csv` (608 distinct event-points) missing** (account `A0000` was absent).
[agent] 2. **Backfilled the missing data.** `hops fg insert transactions --file data/transactions.csv` appended the initial export. The FG then held **673 distinct `(account_id, event_time)` rows = the exact union of both files** (verified against the CSVs; the two files are disjoint).
[agent] 3. **Built a point-in-time feature view** (`churntrainingb2a26a` v1): base = `labels` spine (`account_id`, `label_time`, `churned`), LEFT-joined to all four feature FGs on `account_id`, with `churned` as the label.
[agent] 4. **Materialized training dataset version 1** and read it back. It has **100 rows, one per label**, and the **point-in-time join is correct** — every feature's `event_time ≤ label_time` (spot-checked across rows; nothing leaks from the future).
[agent] ### The blocking limitation
[agent] The task requires **exactly**: `account_id, label_time, amount, balance, credit_score, tier, sessions_7d, health_score, churned`. The delivered TD instead has prefixed columns plus duplicates:
[agent] ```
[agent] account_id, label_time,
[agent] transactions_account_id, transactions_event_time, transactions_amount, transactions_balance,
[agent] profiles_account_id, profiles_event_time, profiles_credit_score, profiles_tier,
[agent] activity_account_id, activity_event_time, activity_sessions_7d,
[agent] account_health_account_id, account_health_event_time, account_health_health_score
[agent] (+ churned as the stored label)
[agent] ```
[agent] **Missing capability: `hops fv create` only supports whole-feature-group joins (`select_all`) — there is no way to select a subset of features or exclude the `event_time`/key columns from each joined FG.** Because point-in-time joins *require* an `event_time` on every source FG, and all four feature FGs share the names `event_time` and `account_id`, the SDK auto-prefixes every joined feature (`transactions_amount` instead of `amount`) and emits four duplicate `*_event_time` and `*_account_id` columns. No combination of `--join` (the optional `[prefix]` only changes the prefix string), `--transform`, or `td compute` options can produce the exact 9-column schema — even renaming the event-time columns to avoid the clash would still leave the four `event_time` columns present, since `select_all` cannot drop them.
[agent] The values and point-in-time correctness are right; the interface simply lacks per-feature selection (`select`/`select_except`) in feature-view creation, which is what's needed to ship the exact column set.
